31. RECURSION
Recursion means:

A function calls itself.

Example:

void fun()
{
    fun();
}
This has no stopping condition.

It can continue until stack/resources are exhausted.

A proper recursive function normally has:

1. Base case
Stops recursion.

2. Recursive case
Calls itself with a smaller/simpler problem.

Example factorial:

5! = 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1
Formula:

n! = n × (n-1)!
Base:

0! = 1
So:

5!
= 5 × 4!
= 5 × 4 × 3!
= 5 × 4 × 3 × 2!
= 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1!
= 120
